<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William R. Bell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1927</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William R. Bell was a British colonial officer who served as district officer of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaita">Malaita</a> in the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Islands <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> from 1915. Known for his firm enforcement of the head tax and of the disarmament of Malaitans, he was killed with his party by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwaio">Kwaio</a> warriors led by Basiana in October 1927 while collecting the tax.</p></div>
